.TH NVIDIA-FLATPAK-NVENC 8 "September 2026" "Remedia" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
nvidia-flatpak-nvenc \- diagnose and restore NVENC in Shotcut Flatpak
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shotcut Flatpak may list the
.B h264_nvenc
encoder but fail to use it with
.BR "Cannot load libcuda.so.1" .
This can happen after an NVIDIA driver update when the Flatpak NVIDIA GL
extension for the loaded driver version is missing. A working
.B nvidia-smi
on the host does not prove that CUDA is available inside the Flatpak.
.PP
This procedure concerns NVENC in Shotcut Flatpak. If
.B nvidia-smi
cannot communicate with the driver, investigate the host driver first;
see
.BR nvidia-display-restore (8).
.SH SYMPTOMS
.IP \(bu 2
MediaPanel export with NVENC fails and reports
.BR "Cannot load libcuda.so.1" .
.IP \(bu 2
.B nvidia-smi
works on the host, but a real NVENC encode in Shotcut Flatpak fails.
.IP \(bu 2
.B ffmpeg -encoders
lists
.B h264_nvenc
inside the Flatpak even though the encoder cannot start.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.SS "Check the host driver and Shotcut installation"
.RS
.nf
nvidia-smi
flatpak info org.shotcut.Shotcut
flatpak --gl-drivers
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read the driver version reported by
.BR nvidia-smi .
The NVIDIA GL extension must match the loaded driver's full version.
For example, driver
.B 595.91.07
corresponds to
.BR org.freedesktop.Platform.GL.nvidia-595-91-07//1.4 .
Installed extensions for older versions do not satisfy this match.
.SS "Derive and check the matching extension"
.RS
.nf
driver_version=$(nvidia-smi --query-gpu=driver_version \
  --format=csv,noheader | sed -n '1p')
if [[ "$driver_version" =~ ^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)+$ ]]; then
  driver_ref="org.freedesktop.Platform.GL.nvidia-${driver_version//./-}//1.4"
  printf '%s\en' "$driver_ref"
  flatpak info "$driver_ref"
else
  printf 'Invalid driver version\en' >&2
fi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run this in Bash. If
.B flatpak info
cannot find the exact reference, check its availability in the configured
Flathub remote before considering an installation. Do not choose a nearby
driver version or hard-code the example version in Doctor.
.SS "Test actual NVENC encoding inside Shotcut Flatpak"
.RS
.nf
flatpak run --command=ffmpeg org.shotcut.Shotcut \
  -hide_banner -f lavfi -i testsrc2=size=640x360:rate=30 \
  -t 1 -c:v h264_nvenc -f null -
printf 'Exit status: %s\en' "$?"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Exit status zero and 30 encoded frames confirm this short test succeeded.
The null output writes no video file. A 128x128 test frame is too small for
some NVIDIA encoders and can produce a misleading failure. Listing encoders
is not an adequate substitute for the encode test.
.SH RECOVERY
.SS "Install the matching extension when available"
If the host driver works, the matching extension is absent, and the user
explicitly requested repair, check the configured Flathub remote:
.RS
.nf
flatpak remote-info flathub "$driver_ref"
.fi
.RE
.PP
If that exact reference is available, install it:
.RS
.nf
flatpak install flathub "$driver_ref"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use the appropriate Flatpak installation scope and configured remote.
Flatpak can have user and system installations; Doctor must identify the
Shotcut installation and avoid treating an extension installed in an
unavailable scope as sufficient. Installation can download a large runtime
and may require authorization. It must not be attempted during audit mode.
.PP
If the exact extension is unavailable or installation fails, report the
reason. Do not install an extension for a different driver version and do
not change the host driver merely to make this Flatpak extension match.
.SH VERIFICATION
Repeat the short 640x360 encode test after installation. If it succeeds,
retry MediaPanel export with NVENC. If it fails, retain the diagnostic output
and let MediaPanel export with
.B libx264
on the CPU. A successful test does not establish that every MLT project or
filter will render successfully; inspect the result of the actual export.
.SH AUTOMATION POLICY
The Remedia Doctor should report the host driver state, loaded driver
version, required and installed Flatpak extension, and the result of a
real NVENC encode. Its default mode is audit and report. It must not infer
NVENC readiness from
.B ffmpeg -encoders
or from
.B nvidia-smi
alone.
.PP
Repair is a separate user-selected action. Before installation, Doctor
must show the exact extension reference and confirm its availability. It
must never install a different driver series, alter the host NVIDIA driver,
or remove older Flatpak extensions as part of this repair. If repair is
unavailable or verification fails, report CPU export as the fallback.
.SH REMEDIA COMMANDS
.RS
.nf
remedia system nvidia-flatpak-nvenc doctor
remedia system nvidia-flatpak-nvenc heal
remedia system nvidia-flatpak-nvenc doctor --scope=system
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run these commands as the desktop user, without sudo. System installation
permissions are requested by Flatpak itself. MediaPanel System Status includes separate NVIDIA Flatpak NVENC Doctor and Heal actions.
The global System Doctor does not run the Shotcut encode test.
.PP
Doctor selects a unique installed Shotcut reference and installation. If
multiple copies or branches exist, use --scope=user, --scope=system or
--scope=NAME, and --branch=BRANCH. Use --remote=REMOTE to select a configured
remote; flathub is the default. No remote is added automatically.
.PP
The audit tests 30 frames at 640x360, with a 45-second timeout. Success
requires exit status zero, 30 frames and a final progress=end record.
If the NVIDIA module is not loaded, nvidia-smi is skipped to avoid implicit
module loading. Diagnose the host first with nvidia-display doctor.
.PP
Heal is offered only when the encode fails, the exact extension is missing
from the selected Shotcut installation, the required GL driver is active,
and the exact architecture/ref is available in the chosen remote.
Confirmation requires the complete short extension reference. Installation
uses --no-related and --no-deps. The host driver and overrides are not
changed; older extensions are not removed. A real encode is repeated after
installation. A matching extension with a failed encode requires manual
investigation, rather than a blind reinstall.
.SH SEE ALSO
nvidia-display-restore(8), nvidia-smi(1), flatpak(1), ffmpeg(1)
.SH AUTHOR
Remedia Project
.SH STATUS
Remedia Doctor/Heal implementation; real-hardware recovery verification remains pending.
